{"timestamp":"2026-06-05T10:57:39Z","event_ts":"2026-06-05T10:57:30Z","repo":"tekkura/sr-firmware","event_name":"issue_comment","action":"created","actor":"topherbuckley","run_id":"27010906073","run_attempt":"1","sender":{"login":"topherbuckley","html_url":"https://github.com/topherbuckley"},"issue":{"number":16,"title":"CC Lines pulled low rather than one floating as expected.","state":"open","html_url":"https://github.com/tekkura/sr-firmware/issues/16","milestone":null,"labels":[]},"milestone":null,"comment":{"id":4630769595,"body":"## 2026-06-05 firmware/bring-up findings\n\nTested MAX77958 behavior with UART diagnostics and temporary firmware changes.\n\n### Firmware changes tested\n- Forced customer config to source mode in RAM.\n- Raised source current advertisement to 1.5 A.\n- Set SID defaults.\n- Explicitly wrote `CC_CTRL1 = 0x82` for source-side CC detection.\n- Handled VBUS enable/disable PD messages in firmware.\n- Temporarily forced GPIO5/GPIO4 high to enable U17 boost and U16 VBUS switch.\n\n### Observations\n- `CC_CTRL1` readback can be forced to `0x82`, so the opcode path is alive.\n- With phone attached and source-only CC control active, `CC_STATUS0` stayed at `state=0` or later `state=6`; it never reached `state=2` source attach.\n- `PD_STATUS0` stayed `0x00`; no PD message flow occurred.\n- Forcing GPIO4/GPIO5 high produced `GPIO53=0x0f`, confirming U16/U17 can be firmware-enabled.\n- Forced VBUS charged/woke the phone only while the phone was off. Once Android booted, charging stopped.\n- This matches the earlier measurements showing both CC lines pulled/clamped low.\n\n### Conclusion\nThe blocking fault does not appear to be the VBUS switch/boost firmware path. The board can force 5 V onto phone VBUS, but Android rejects or stops charging because the Type-C CC attach layer never becomes valid. The MAX77958 never advertises/detects a valid source attach, so PD never starts.\n\nCurrent evidence points to the MAX77958 CC pins/path being clamped, damaged, or forced into a protection/disabled state. Next hardware work should focus on the isolated USB-PD prototype and CC-line behavior around U11, ESD/caps, and J4 before spending more time on firmware policy.","html_url":"https://github.com/tekkura/sr-firmware/issues/16#issuecomment-4630769595"}}
