{"timestamp":"2026-06-18T09:55:41Z","event_ts":"2026-06-18T09:55:29Z","repo":"tekkura/sr-firmware","event_name":"issue_comment","action":"created","actor":"topherbuckley","run_id":"27751534661","run_attempt":"1","sender":{"login":"topherbuckley","html_url":"https://github.com/topherbuckley"},"issue":{"number":14,"title":"Feature/versioning","state":"open","html_url":"https://github.com/tekkura/sr-firmware/pull/14","milestone":null,"labels":[]},"milestone":null,"comment":{"id":4740726712,"body":"Updated in `b24af6a`.\n\nWhat changed:\n- Aligned `VERSIONING_IMPLEMENTATION.md` with the implemented wire contract: `GET_VERSION` returns a framed response whose payload is exactly three unsigned bytes (`major`, `minor`, `patch`), not a SemVer string.\n- Added a header guard to `include/version.h`.\n\nWhy:\n- The Android and firmware PRs now agree on the binary version payload, and the docs no longer describe a conflicting string-based response format.","html_url":"https://github.com/tekkura/sr-firmware/pull/14#issuecomment-4740726712"}}
